on real ES 1m 2010-2026. Rules are FROZEN from their validated standalone tests —
zero re-tuning here. This measures what the surviving edges do TOGETHER on $1k.

  A. Bull-regime overnight drift (overnight_edge.py):
       at 16:00 ET, if price > 200d MA (MA of closes through YESTERDAY — strictly
       causal), long 1 MES to next 09:30. Skips Friday (>24h gap), no stop.
  B. Overreaction fade (OverreactionFade.pine spec):
       after an RTH day with |open->close| > 1.2 x session-ATR(14), fade at next
       09:30 open: target 0.5xATR, stop 0.7xATR, flat by close. 15m exec.
  C. Pre-FOMC drift (box_theory/fomc.py):
       long D-1 16:00 ET -> D 13:59 ET, scheduled meetings only.

Each sleeve trades 1 MES. Costs INCLUDED ($2.5 RT for A/B, $5.0 for C).
Reports: per-sleeve + combined ann$, maxDD, Calmar (full window AND rolling 3y —
the 3y number is the apples-to-apples one vs industry backtests), Sharpe,
signals/week, sleeve correlations, Monte-Carlo P(ruin) on $1k.
"""
