"""
vp_value_area.py — Volume-Profile / Value-Area intraday strategy, faithful build.

Trader's thesis:
  Value area = price band holding 70% of a session's volume (VAL..VAH around POC).
  A) REJECTION REVERSAL: price poked OUTSIDE prior value area but CLOSED back inside
     -> fade back toward POC (mean revert).
  B) BREAKOUT + FVG RETEST: price CLOSED decisively beyond the value area and left a
     fair-value gap in the impulse leg; when price wicks back into the gap, ride the
     continuation in the breakout direction.

CAUSAL DISCIPLINE (paranoid about lookahead):
  - Value area = PRIOR completed RTH session only (known before today's open).
  - Every signal is decided at a bar's CLOSE; entry is the NEXT bar's OPEN (M.evaluate
    enters at open[entry_bar]).
  - Exit bar = first bar whose HIGH/LOW touches stop or target (decided at that bar's
    close); if a single bar straddles BOTH, assume STOP first (conservative). Else force
    exit at the last RTH bar (16:00). M.evaluate values the exit at close[exit_bar]
    (open->close harness), so stop/target only choose WHICH bar we exit on — the fill is
    the bar close, an honest (non-optimistic) approximation, never the exact stop price.
  - FVG uses only bars (p-2,p-1,p) all <= current; retest & breakout decided at close.
  - Single-position book: never two open trades at once (a $1k / 1-micro account).

Usage: python3 vp_value_area.py
