#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""OCEAN family f12_exit_engine — EXIT engineering on a FIXED principled entry (MES 1-lot).

This family searches EXITS ONLY. The entry is frozen (no entry parameter is tuned):

  BASE ENTRY (house reference = omni4_preserve.sim_day, first-breakout branch,
  er_thr=0.40, max_entries=1, use_atr_stop=True, atr_mult=1.5):
    * Scan completed 5-min bars b = 6 .. 76 (after the 09:30-10:00 opening range,
      never entering on the last bar).
    * ER gate: continuous efficiency ratio ER(24) at bar b must be >= 0.40.
    * LONG  if close[b] > or_hi AND close[b] > vwap[b]  (first such gated bar);
      SHORT if close[b] < or_lo AND close[b] < vwap[b].
    * Fill at that bar's close (market; slippage inside friction).
    * Initial stop = entry -/+ max(1.5*ATR(b), 5.0 pts) (omni2_lib FLOOR).
    * Max 1 entry per day; sessions independent.

  EXIT SCHEMES compared (the only thing swept):
    (a) eod    — incumbent: hold to 16:00 bar-77 close (initial stop stays live).
    (b) chan k — chandelier trail: after each completed bar, high-water-mark of the
        favorable extreme (starts at entry price) minus/plus k*ATR(bar); stop only
        ratchets in the trade's favor; the updated level applies from the NEXT bar.
        k in {2,3,4}.
    (c) be k   — breakeven-after-1R then trail: initial stop until the favorable
        extreme has moved >= 1.0*initial-risk from entry (checked at bar close);
        then stop = max(entry, HWM - k*ATR) (mirrored for shorts), ratchet only.
        k in {2,3,4}.
    (d) time N — exit at the close of bar entry+N (market, eod friction); initial
        stop live until then. N in {6,12,24}.
    (e) target R — resting limit at entry +/- R*initial-risk (fric("target")=0.41,
        no exit slippage); initial stop live; if stop and target both touched in
        one bar the STOP is taken (conservative). R in {1.5, 2.0, 3.0}.

  All exits: stop checked intrabar only on bars strictly AFTER the entry bar;
  any trail/BE level computed at the close of bar b binds from bar b+1 onward;
  EOD exit at bar-77 close with fric("eod")=0.66 pt.

FAMILY VERDICT RULE (fixed before running): CANDIDATE only if one non-EOD scheme
beats the eod-ride on MAR (net/|maxDD|) in >= 3 of 4 DEV eras
(2010-13, 2014-17, 2018-21, 2022), sits on a plateau (every immediate grid
neighbor of its exit parameter DEV-net-positive), and passes the DEV survival bar.

Windows: dev = dates <= 2022-12-31; holdout = 2023-01-01..; all. Holdout is
