Builds a clean continuous ES front-month from the GLBX parent ohlcv-1m file
(outrights only, volume-based roll, DST-aware New York sessions), then tests
whether the LAST-30-min return is predicted by the FIRST-30-min (and overnight)
return -- gross, full-sample vs post-publication (2018-07), with HAC and
circular block-bootstrap significance. No strategy code, no fitting: a falsifier.

Then layers retail cost economics for a $1,000 and $5,000 account.

