#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
scout_regime.py  --  Causal TREND vs MEAN-REVERSION regime classifier for NQ intraday.

QUESTION: can you know, BEFORE the session, whether today will trend or chop?
If not, a routed dual-playbook ("catch reversions AND trends") cannot work.

Design
------
LABEL (future data, evaluation only):
    ER = |close-open| / (high-low) over the labelled window.
    TREND if ER > 0.6, RANGE if ER < 0.3, MIXED otherwise.
    Window A ("full")   = 09:30 -> 16:00 ET   (paired with features known at 09:30)
    Window B ("post10") = 10:00 -> 16:00 ET   (paired with features known at 10:00,
                                               so the opening range is NOT inside the label)

FEATURES: all computed from bars strictly BEFORE the anchor timestamp, via a
generic anchor-relative builder (the same builder is reused for the random-time
placebo). Every rolling stat is sampled at bar (p-1), i.e. the last bar that has
CLOSED before the anchor.

ADVERSARIAL NOTES ON THE SUPPLIED COLUMNS
    * atr15/atr30/atr60 in nq_v5.parquet change only on 15/30/60-min boundaries and
      are ffilled from the resampled bar's LEFT label -> the value at 18:30 was
      computed using bars up to 18:45. LOOKAHEAD. Not used; own 1-min causal vol
      estimators are built instead.
    * bear_*/bull_* flags + bear_score/bull_score have the same construction
      (state computed on a resampled bar, stamped at that bar's OPEN, ffilled).
      bear_daily flips at 18:00/19:00 using the whole day-cycle's data; bear_weekly
      carries up to a week of lookahead. Own causal SSMT states are rebuilt here,
      stamped at bar CLOSE. The supplied score is fed in only as a labelled
      "CONTAMINATED" diagnostic so the lookahead inflation can be measured.

SPLITS   IS = NQ 2023-01-01..2024-12-31 | OOS1 = NQ 2025+ | OOS2 = MNQ 2026
COSTS    NQ  pv=20 $4.00 RT  0.25pt slip on entry and on stop exits
         MNQ pv=2  $1.50 RT  same
Entries at NEXT bar open. Stop-before-target inside a bar. Flat by 16:59.
"""
